      "writtenOn": "2019-08-16T07:43:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Haven\u0027t checked but since prefer_idle is a per-task thing, can\u0027t you use only the existing max_spare_cap{_cpu}?\n\nif ((!prefer_idle || !idle_cpu()) \u0026\u0026 (spare_cap \u003e max_spare_cap)) {\n\tmax_spare_cap \u003d spare_cap;\n\tmax_spare_cap_cpu \u003d cpu;\n}\n\namong other little tweaks? Max spare and highest spare should be the same, just on a different set of Cpus.",
      "parentUuid": "c0bfd98d_edc81b81",
      "revId": "4b4f1a7f2b905ac93a5c4bfdc0bf4787c38c6ec2",
