      "writtenOn": "2019-08-16T10:29:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe better:\n\n   highest_spare_cap_cpu \u003d\u003e max_spare_cap_cpu_pi\n   highest_spare_cap     \u003d\u003e max_spare_cap_pi\n\nWhere the \"_pi\" at the end refers to \"prefer_idle\" case?\n\nEven better, looking at the changed I\u0027ve linked below, it seems to be possible to re-use the `max_spare_cap{_cpu}` variables we already have. Indeed, if I\u0027m not wrong, we never need to use both `max_spare_cap*` and `highest_spare_cap*`, do we?",
      "parentUuid": "6c8350af_c2290230",
      "revId": "4b4f1a7f2b905ac93a5c4bfdc0bf4787c38c6ec2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
